{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100694 :question/math-academy-id "e-4406" :question/problem "Find $CD$, if \n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\nand \n\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nCD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101102 :question/math-academy-id "q-1029" :question/problem "If\n$X = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$Y = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nthen $XY =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101104 :question/math-academy-id "q-1034" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ 9 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237990 :question/math-academy-id "q-1033" :question/problem "If\n$E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$F=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nthen $EF=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $E$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $F$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $E$ and $4$ rows in $F,$ so $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={EF}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $EF,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=1\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,18=1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,15=3\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,9=3\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$EF=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238011 :question/math-academy-id "q-1035" :question/problem "Find $ST$,  if  $S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ matrix and $T$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $T,$ so $S$ and $T$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{T}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={ST}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $ST,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,24=2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$ST=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265743 :question/math-academy-id "q-129495" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=2\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,3=2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-9=1\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 6+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,10=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265744 :question/math-academy-id "q-129496" :question/problem "Find $XY$,  if  $X=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $X$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $Y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $X$ and $3$ rows in $Y,$ so $X$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={XY}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $XY,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,22=5\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,9=5\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$XY=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299650 :question/math-academy-id "q-317844" :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $9$ |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} | $14$ |  |  |\n|  | $5$ | {{field-5}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}={AB}_{4\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 9 \\\\ ∗ & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ ∗ & 9 \\\\ ∗ & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ ∗ & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,0=0\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=(-1)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=5\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299651 :question/math-academy-id "q-317846" :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $9$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & -8\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-3=1\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -8\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-8=0\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299652 :question/math-academy-id "q-317847" :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,5=2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,7=4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299653 :question/math-academy-id "q-317848" :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $11$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-2=4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338850 :question/math-academy-id "q-70928" :question/problem "Find $BC$,  if  $B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $B$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $C$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $C,$ so $B$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={BC}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $BC,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-10=(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -14\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-14=(-3)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$BC=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100873 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100695 :question/math-academy-id "e-4407" :question/problem "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $A$ by the $2$nd column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101529 :question/math-academy-id "q-70791" :question/problem "Let $C = AB$. What is the value of $c_{13}$, if\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101530 :question/math-academy-id "q-70792" :question/problem "Let $Z = XY$. What is the value of $z_{42}$, if\n$X = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}, Y = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265828 :question/math-academy-id "q-130111" :question/problem "Let $S=UV.$ What is the value of ${s}_{13}$, if\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $1$st row in $U$ by the $3$rd column in $V$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{13} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-6-6+5 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265831 :question/math-academy-id "q-130120" :question/problem "Let $D=AB.$ What is the value of ${d}_{24}$, if\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $A$ by the $4$th column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{24} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-9+4+3 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292866 :question/math-academy-id "q-275547" :question/problem "Let $L=MN.$ What is the value of ${l}_{22}$, if\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${l}_{22}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $M$ by the $2$nd column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{l}_{22} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8+6 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299685 :question/math-academy-id "q-318462" :question/problem "Let $P=QR.$ What is the value of ${p}_{31}$, if\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${p}_{31}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $Q$ by the $1$st column in $R$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{31} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2(5)+1(-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\  & =10-3-2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299686 :question/math-academy-id "q-318463" :question/problem "Let $X=YZ.$ What is the value of ${x}_{12}$, if\n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${x}_{12}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $1$st row in $Y$ by the $2$nd column in $Z$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)(5)+3(-3)+0(1) \\\\  & =-10-9+0 \\\\  & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299687 :question/math-academy-id "q-318470" :question/problem "Let $Z=XY.$ What is the value of ${z}_{24}$, if\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${z}_{24}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $X$ by the $4$th column in $Y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{24} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3(-3)+2(2) \\\\  & =-9+4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338852 :question/math-academy-id "q-70946" :question/problem "Let $D=EF.$ What is the value of ${d}_{23}$, if\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,F=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $E$ by the $3$rd column in $F$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{23} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-5)+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =20-6 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338853 :question/math-academy-id "q-70949" :question/problem "Let $K=MN.$ What is the value of ${k}_{12}$, if\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,N=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $1$st row in $M$ by the $2$nd column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}_{12} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-5+8 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338855 :question/math-academy-id "q-70956" :question/problem "Let $T=UV.$ What is the value of ${t}_{41}$, if\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 10 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 20 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $4$th row of $U$ by the $1$st column in $V$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{41} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 10 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 20 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot (-1)+10\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =10-3-10 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338856 :question/math-academy-id "q-70958" :question/problem "Let $R=PQ.$ What is the value of ${r}_{25}$, if\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $2$nd row of $P$ by the $5$th column of $Q$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{25} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 10+(-4)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =30-28 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Entry of the Product of Two Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100913 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100741 :question/math-academy-id "e-5885" :question/problem "Compute the product \n $\\begin{bmatrix}\n       -1  \\\\\n \t0  \\\\\n        -2\n \t\n    \\end{bmatrix}\n\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n        2 & -5\n    \\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} {\\color{green}\\checkmark} {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} = \n\t\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n       -1  \\\\\n \t0  \\\\\n        -2\n    \\end{bmatrix}\n\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n        2 & -5\n    \\end{bmatrix}\n\n\t&= \n\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n        (-1)\\cdot 2 & (-1)\\cdot (-5)  \\\\\n        0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot (-5) \\\\\n        (-2)\\cdot 2 & (-2)\\cdot (-5)\n    \\end{bmatrix} \\\\[5pt]\n\n\t&=\n\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n       -2 & 5  \\\\\n       0 &  0  \\\\\n       -4 &  10 \n    \\end{bmatrix} \n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101103 :question/math-academy-id "q-1031" :question/problem "What is $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101140 :question/math-academy-id "q-13636" :question/problem "Find $CD$, if\n$C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$D = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238054 :question/math-academy-id "q-1038" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10\\cdot 1 & -10\\cdot (-5) & -10\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 6\\cdot 1 & 6\\cdot (-5) & 6\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 8\\cdot 1 & 8\\cdot (-5) & 8\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265792 :question/math-academy-id "q-129961" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nthen $AB=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-3=-1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-9=(-3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,3=(-3)\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265838 :question/math-academy-id "q-130136" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\cdot 1 & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 4 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265857 :question/math-academy-id "q-130230" :question/problem "Find $ST$, if \n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$T=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $T$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $S$ and $2$ rows in $T$, so the product is undefined:\n\n$$\n{S}_{3\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{2\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292865 :question/math-academy-id "q-275545" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $AB.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=2\\cdot -2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=-1\\cdot -2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-3=-1\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292867 :question/math-academy-id "q-275548" :question/problem "Find $AB,$ if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299688 :question/math-academy-id "q-318484" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $AB.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,5=5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-2=-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=-2\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299689 :question/math-academy-id "q-318588" :question/problem "Find $PQ,$ if\n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $PQ=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $P$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $Q$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $P$ and $1$ row in matrix $Q$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Q}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={PQ}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot (-4) & 0\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-4) & 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-4) & (-1)\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396025 :question/math-academy-id "q-13635" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 1 & (-3)\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector"}] :topic/title "Multiplying Matrices"}
